.SS "def birda_process_wav\&.add_metadata_to_csv ( csv_file,  latitude,  longitude,  recording_start,  timezone)"

.PP
Rewrite a results CSV with coordinates and derived detection timestamps\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcsv_file\fP Existing Birda results CSV, replaced after successful processing\&. 
.br
\fIlatitude\fP Signed latitude in decimal degrees\&. 
.br
\fIlongitude\fP Signed longitude in decimal degrees\&. 
.br
\fIrecording_start\fP Naive recording-local datetime from the WAV basename\&. 
.br
\fItimezone\fP IANA timezone label written to every row\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Number of enriched detection rows\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExceptions\fP
.RS 4
\fISystemExit\fP Raised for CSV validation failures\&. 
.br
\fIOSError\fP Raised for unhandled write or replacement failures\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
detection_time equals recording_start plus the row's Start (s)\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
Validation exits can leave the fixed \&.tmp file behind\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
Add/fill:

    lat
    lon
    detection_time
    timezone

detection_time is:

    recording_start + Start (s)

Example:

    2026-01-26 20:14:33
    Australia/Sydney
.fi
.PP
 
